      "message": "Unless I misunderstand how this code is supposed to work, I think this is not what you intended.\n\n`sk_sp\u003cSkRuntimeEffect\u003e` is an intermediate object, the result of calling `SkRuntimeEffect::MakeForBlender` (or `MakeForShader`/`MakeForColorFilter`). This contains a compiled version of your SkSL but is not associated with any uniforms or children yet. Users are supposed to take that object and call `myRuntimeEffect-\u003emakeBlender(myUniforms, myChildren)` on it to create a fully formed `sk_sp\u003cSkBlender\u003e` object that can be attached to a SkPaint. (This allows compiled code to be re-bound to different uniforms and children more efficiently)\n\nInternally that blender object will always be a `sk_sp\u003cSkRuntimeBlender\u003e` but that class isn\u0027t exposed anywhere outside of `SkRuntimeEffect`. (We can make it visible to Graphite if necessary, but I don\u0027t know if that will help; virtual functions should be sufficient AFAICS.) You can also use the Flattenable system to identify runtime shaders/blenders via `getTypeName()`.",
